## Materialized views carry `pipelines.externalMetadata.enabled` (MV change feed enabler)
================================================================================

Context: the public docs now describe the materialized-view change feed as a
Beta enabled by a table property rather than a private-preview enrolment:
`'pipelines.externalMetadata.enabled' = 'true'` in the view's TBLPROPERTIES
("external data access to streaming tables and materialized views"). The
`_data` and `_graph` views are what the net-change apply and an MV-sourced
Lakebase synced table read the change feed of, so they carry the property.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py — `_MV_HEADER`
   adds `'pipelines.externalMetadata.enabled' = 'true'` next to the preview
   channel and row tracking (the definition fingerprint does not cover
   properties, so existing views are not recreated for it; they get it on
   their next `CREATE OR REPLACE`).
2. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_materialized_view_builder.py — the pinned
   DDL carries the property.
3. docs/incremental-materialization.md — Preview enrolment: the property, and
   the live result.

Live (2026-11-03, fevm-ontobricks-int, fixture view dropped afterwards): with
the property, `REPAIR TABLE … SYNC METADATA` succeeds (it was refused with
`REPAIR_TABLE_REQUIRES_EXTERNAL_METADATA` without it), so the flag is honoured;
`SHOW TBLPROPERTIES` does not echo it; `DESCRIBE HISTORY` / `DESCRIBE DETAIL`
still answer `EXPECT_TABLE_NOT_VIEW`, and `table_changes` fails with
`DELTA_LOG_FILE_NOT_FOUND … _external_metadata/_delta_log` for the full ten
minutes of polling with refreshes and repairs — the external metadata is not
produced on that workspace yet (the view's DBSQL pipeline cannot be
reconfigured: "Pipeline type 'DBSQL' is not supported"). The feed therefore
stays unreadable there and every caller falls back as documented.

