## Live Real-Time Mode run: realtime p99 244 ms; the sink and processor accept RTM's tuple rows
================================================================================

Context: the design's `realtime` KPI (Kafka event → Lakebase p99 < 1 s) needed
classic DBR 19 compute and a topic. An FEVM `aws_sandbox_classic` workspace
(`ontobricks-rtm`, us-east-1, created with the user's go-ahead) with a classic
cluster, a KRaft Kafka broker on the driver and a Lakebase instance of its own
ran the processing leg in Real-Time Mode.

Measured (2026-11-03): 20 events/s for 150 s (2 982 events, 28 deletes, 200
keys), `trigger(realTime="1 minute")`, three real-time batches back to back,
400 live rows + 4 tombstones; end-to-end latency (event `ts_ms` → Postgres
`updated_at`) **p50 185 ms, p95 234 ms, p99 244 ms, max 246 ms** (n = 198).
The KPI is met.

Found live, fixed here:

1. src/jobs/triple_stream/LiveSink.py — under the real-time trigger `foreach`
   hands the writer a plain tuple in the output schema's column order
   (`LIVE_COLUMNS`), not a `Row`: `values` accepts a `Row`, a mapping or a
   tuple (the live failure was `dict(tuple)`:
   "dictionary update sequence element #0 has length 16").
2. src/jobs/triple_stream/processor.py — `_as_dict` accepts a tuple in
   `ENVELOPE_FIELDS` order for the same reason.
3. tests/units/jobs/test_triple_stream_processor.py,
   tests/units/jobs/test_triple_stream_main.py — tuple rows through the
   processor and the sink; an unreadable row type is refused.
4. docs/incremental-materialization.md — Live verification (the run, the
   numbers, the platform findings below), traceability (Processing row live,
   KPI row realtime ✅).

Found live, recorded (fixed in the next section): Real-Time Mode refuses the
`mapInPandas` envelope explode of `main.py`
(`STREAMING_REAL_TIME_MODE.OPERATOR_OR_SINK_NOT_IN_ALLOWLIST: MapInPandasExec`;
with the allowlist check off it fails with `ClassCastException …
RealTimeIterator`), and it schedules every stage at once, so the cluster needs
source + shuffle partitions free task slots (`CONCURRENT_SCHEDULER_INSUFFICIENT_SLOT`
with the default 200 shuffle partitions).

