## Registry delete by display name addresses the sanitised folder
================================================================================

Context: found by scenario 06's cleanup on the sandbox app. `DELETE
/settings/registry/domains/ZzIncrementalLive` answered 200 "deleted from
registry" and the domain stayed listed: the registry stores the sanitised
folder (`zzincrementallive`, `sanitize_domain_folder`), the Lakebase `DELETE …
WHERE folder = 'ZzIncrementalLive'` matched no row and the Volume path with the
display name did not exist, so nothing was deleted and no error was raised
(`recursive_delete: … /domains/ZzIncrementalLive does not exist, skipping` in
the app log). The registry UI passes the folder and never hit it; API callers
and the campaign suites pass the name.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/domain/settings/RegistryDomainSettings.py —
   `delete_registry_domain_result` and `delete_registry_version_result`
   resolve `sanitize_domain_folder(domain_name)` once (idempotent on a folder)
   and use it for every store call (`list_versions`, `read_version`,
   `delete_version`, `delete_domain`, the loaded-domain check, the GitHub
   mirror); messages keep the name the caller sent.
2. tests/units/settings/test_v090_settings_registry_domains.py — a display
   name with a space and a dash deletes `zz_incremental_live`; the version
   delete addresses every store call with the folder.
