## A failed slot update owes the next one a full refresh (`slot_update_failed`)
================================================================================

Context: scenario 06's second journey on the sandbox app re-created
`ZzIncrementalLive` V1 after the registry delete, which keeps the graph
artefacts: the build adopted the former slot pipeline (same SQL fingerprint)
and its update resumed the old checkpoint. Between the two incarnations the
`untracked` fixture's row tracking had been turned off and on again, so the
change-feed stream failed on that version range
(`DELTA_MISSING_ROW_TRACKING_FOR_CDC … ontobricks_rtm_catalog.rtm.untracked`,
flow failed more than 2 times, update FAILED) and the build fell back as
designed (`mode_fallback_reason: incremental_failed:InfrastructureError`,
`strategy: merge`, effective `incremental`, 6 triples). But the run recorded
`slot_full_refresh_pending: false`, so every later build would resume the same
checkpoint and fall back again — a sticky failure.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py — `_build` wraps
   the slot update: an `OntoBricksError` from it marks the recorded facts
   `slot_full_refresh_pending: true`, `slot_full_refresh_reason:
   slot_update_failed` (an already-owed reason stays), then re-raises into the
   fallback ladder; `TwinSlotRefreshPlan.owed` already honours any recorded
   reason, so the next update runs as a full refresh.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinSlotRefreshPlan.py —
   `REASON_SLOT_UPDATE_FAILED`; the reasons docstring.
3. tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_net_apply.py — a failed update with
   nothing owed records `slot_update_failed`, pending; the existing test keeps
   `source_overwritten` when that was already owed.
4. docs/incremental-materialization.md — the reason in the Reconciliation text
   and the trace-row table; Known limitations: a re-created domain adopts its
   former pipeline and checkpoint (drop the pipeline first for a clean first
   build; follow-up: delete a domain's pipeline and tables with the domain).

Not done, on purpose: forcing a full refresh whenever a pipeline is adopted
without slot history in the domain's runs — some twenty-five build tests encode
"an adopted pipeline running the current SQL resumes incrementally", and the
proper fix is the artefact cleanup on domain delete.

