## Sandbox deploy notes (`ontobricks-rtm`, no code change)
================================================================================

Context: the UI and MCP apps were deployed to the FEVM `aws_sandbox_classic`
workspace `ontobricks-rtm` (profile `ontobricks-rtm`, `DEFAULT_INSTANCE_ID=rtm`,
registry `ontobricks_rtm_catalog.ontobricks_rtm_registry`, Lakebase project
`ontobricks-rtm`) to run the deployed-app journey (scenario 06). Recorded for
whoever deploys to a sandbox again; nothing in the repository changed for it.

1. The sandbox rejects `user_api_scopes` on apps: the two blocks were removed
   from a working copy of `databricks.yml` for the deploy and restored
   afterwards (`git checkout databricks.yml`); the rendered `app.yaml` files
   were reused with `--skip-app-yaml`.
2. `scripts/deploy.sh --no-bootstrap` (psql is not installed here) leaves the
   apps' own service principals without `CAN_MANAGE` on themselves after every
   deploy — the bundle's `permissions` block replaces the ACL — so every page
   answers `/access-denied?reason=bootstrap` until `databricks apps
   update-permissions <app> --json '{"access_control_list":[{"service_principal_name":
   "<app client id>","permission_level":"CAN_MANAGE"}]}'` is run for both apps
   (what `make bootstrap-perms` does).
3. New managed tables on that workspace carry `delta.enableRowTracking=true` by
   default: the "untracked" fixture of scenario 06 has to be set to `false`
   explicitly before a run, and the readiness probe then reports it as untracked.
4. `databricks apps logs <app> --tail-lines 0 --search <build id>` recovers a
   build's full log after the default 200-line window has moved on.

